WEBVTT

00:03:58.746 --> 00:04:02.454
we might have seen the inauguration
of ruler K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo',

00:04:02.496 --> 00:04:05.704
roughly translated, that means
Sun-Faced First Macaw.

00:04:05.746 --> 00:04:07.663
The Maya rulers had really great names:

00:04:07.704 --> 00:04:11.204
Bird Jaguar, Dark Sun, Lady Great Skull.

00:04:11.246 --> 00:04:14.038
But what was really neat
about Yax K'uk' Mo'

00:04:14.079 --> 00:04:18.413
is that he established a dynasty
that lasted for more than 400 years.

00:04:18.454 --> 00:04:21.663
And every depiction
we have of him, as you see here,

00:04:21.704 --> 00:04:23.371
shows him in foreign clothing.

00:04:23.413 --> 00:04:25.621
This is what people wore
in central Mexico,

00:04:25.663 --> 00:04:29.413
which was not in the Maya region
and actually hundreds of miles away.

00:04:29.454 --> 00:04:33.663
So for a long time, archaeologists thought
that this was a foreign king.